<title>USA: Perio Products, General Medical withdraw IPOs.</title>
<headline>Perio Products, General Medical withdraw IPOs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lead underwriter Smith Barney Inc confirmed the withdrawal of initial public offerings of Perio Products Ltd and General Medical Inc.</p>
<p>General Medical, a supplier of health care supplies, terminated the IPO after it got an offer to be acquired by McKesson Corp for $775 million. It had filed to offer nine million shares for $16 to $18.</p>
<p>Perio Products Ltd pulled its IPO until it could get approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The company's Perio chip is aimed at fighting gum disease.</p>
</text>
